<title>USA: Chicago mayor urges plan on school funding - report.</title>
<headline>Chicago mayor urges plan on school funding - report.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Mayor Richard Daley said Tuesday that he sent a letter urging Illinois Gov. Jim Edgar to work on school funding, according to a report in Wednesday's Chicago Sun-Times.</p>
<p>The newspaper reported that the mayor wants the governor to push through an income tax hike in the General Assembly in exchange for property tax relief.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, Edgar has said he plans to propose a major school finance reform plan in his upcoming state of the state address, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
